    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Problem:** in Sia's Emacs the box titles and entries could not be walked: `keycast-log-mode` showed `TAB` and `<right>` running `sp-dashboard-next-button` and `sp-dashboard-enter-box`, but nothing moved.\n\n**Likely cause (not reproduced):** `sp-dashboard-refresh` was on `window-state-change-hook` and `window-configuration-change-hook`, and it kills and redraws the Dashboard every time they run. Those hooks also run for reasons other than a resize (a key logger, the mode line, a message). A redraw puts point back on the first title and out of any box, so each key press is undone at once.\n\n**Change:**\n- The hooks now call `sp-dashboard--refresh-on-resize`, which redraws only when the pixel size of the window or the font differs from the last draw (`sp-dashboard--drawn-geometry`, set when the mode starts). `sp-dashboard-refresh` itself is unchanged for the other callers (`g`, art moves, privacy changes).\n- The width of the larger box titles is read with `window-font-width` instead of `string-pixel-width`, so nothing is measured in a temporary buffer on each draw.\n- Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n**Checked:** Emacs 29.3 headless: running both window hooks after TAB and `<right>` keeps point and the box; a real resize still redraws. Graphical Emacs 29.3 on a virtual display with a window manager and real Tab, S-Tab, Right and Left key presses (xdotool), through the real startup hooks and `sp-set-window-margins`: everything works, titles stay aligned. **Not checked:** Sia's Emacs (31, Mac), real nerd-icons, keycast. I could not reproduce the failure here, so this may not be the whole cause.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
